            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-COMFASTERXMLJACKSONCORE-17434790",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Server-side Request Forgery (SSRF) vulnerability in com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-54514) com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind@2.15.4"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind) is a library which contains the general-purpose data-binding functionality and tree-model for Jackson Data Processor.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Server-side Request Forgery (SSRF) in the `JDKFromStringDeserializer` class, which constructs `InetSocketAddress` and resolves the hostname through DNS at deserialization time. An attacker can force the server to issue outbound DNS lookups for chosen hostnames by submitting JSON that is deserialized into a type holding an `InetSocketAddress` field, with no authentication required. The observable effect is limited to DNS resolution of attacker-chosen names, useful for out-of-band interaction or internal resolver probing rather than a full outbound request, and it applies only where the application deserializes untrusted JSON into types containing such fields.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind` to version 2.18.8, 2.21.4 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Advisory](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/security/advisories/GHSA-hgj6-7826-r7m5)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/commit/1f5a1037b1e9e05920e755cb35f198bcd46667e4)\n- [GitHub PR](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/pull/5951)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-918",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.9,
                "security-severity": "6.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-COMFASTERXMLJACKSONCORE-17440366",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Incomplete List of Disallowed Inputs vulnerability in com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-54513) com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind@2.15.4"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind) is a library which contains the general-purpose data-binding functionality and tree-model for Jackson Data Processor.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Incomplete List of Disallowed Inputs in the `BasicPolymorphicTypeValidator.Builder.allowIfSubTypeIsArray()` method, which allowlists an array based only on `clazz.isArray()` and does not validate the array's component type. An attacker who controls the deserialized JSON can instantiate types outside the configured allowlist by wrapping them in an array, because array elements without per-element type identifiers are constructed directly with no further validator check.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind` to version 2.18.8, 2.21.4 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Advisory](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/security/advisories/GHSA-rmj7-2vxq-3g9f)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/commit/01d1692c8d0ed03e51a0e3c4f8a9e6908e4931e5)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/commit/24529da29fdf46ff94ca38de9ebf31cd188f5e8e)\n- [GitHub Issue](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/issues/5981)\n- [GitHub Issue](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/issues/5983)\n- [GitHub PR](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/pull/5984)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-184",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.2,
                "security-severity": "9.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-COMFASTERXMLJACKSONCORE-17440598",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Deserialization of Untrusted Data vulnerability in com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-54512) com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind@2.15.4"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind) is a library which contains the general-purpose data-binding functionality and tree-model for Jackson Data Processor.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Deserialization of Untrusted Data in the `DatabindContext._resolveAndValidateGeneric()` method, which validates only the raw container class of a type identifier against the configured `PolymorphicTypeValidator` and not its nested generic type arguments. An attacker who controls the type identifier can instantiate a denied class, and reach unauthenticated remote code execution through an available gadget, by embedding that class as a generic parameter of an allowlisted container such as `java.util.ArrayList<com.evil.Gadget>`, which passes validation while the nested type is loaded, instantiated, and populated with attacker-controlled values. Exploitation requires polymorphic type validation to be enabled with a configured validator, the application to deserialize untrusted JSON, and a suitable gadget class on the classpath.\n\n## Details\n\nSerialization is a process of converting an object into a sequence of bytes which can be persisted to a disk or database or can be sent through streams. The reverse process of creating object from sequence of bytes is called deserialization. Serialization is commonly used for communication (sharing objects between multiple hosts) and persistence (store the object state in a file or a database). It is an integral part of popular protocols like _Remote Method Invocation (RMI)_, _Java Management Extension (JMX)_, _Java Messaging System (JMS)_, _Action Message Format (AMF)_, _Java Server Faces (JSF) ViewState_, etc.\n\n_Deserialization of untrusted data_ ([CWE-502](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/502.html)) is when the application deserializes untrusted data without sufficiently verifying that the resulting data will be valid, thus allowing the attacker to control the state or the flow of the execution.\n  \n## Remediation\nUpgrade `com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind` to version 2.18.8, 2.21.4 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Advisory](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/security/advisories/GHSA-j3rv-43j4-c7qm)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/commit/434d6c511de7fdd9872f29157aafb6162d12d8d5)\n- [GitHub Issue](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/issues/5988)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-184",
                  "CWE-502",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.2,
                "security-severity": "9.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-COMFASTERXMLJACKSONCORE-17457695",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Improperly Controlled Modification of Dynamically-Determined Object Attributes vulnerability in com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-54515) com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind@2.15.4"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind) is a library which contains the general-purpose data-binding functionality and tree-model for Jackson Data Processor.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improperly Controlled Modification of Dynamically-Determined Object Attributes in the `BeanDeserializerBase.createContextual()` method, which applies the per-property exclusions through `_handleByNameInclusion()` and then rebuilds the property map from the unfiltered original, overwriting the filtered map and restoring every property the exclusion had removed. An attacker can set fields that were marked ignored, enabling mass assignment, by supplying those property names in untrusted JSON during deserialization. Exploitation requires case-insensitive property matching to be enabled via `@JsonFormat` with `ACCEPT_CASE_INSENSITIVE_PROPERTIES` alongside per-property `@JsonIgnoreProperties`.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind` to version 2.18.9, 2.21.5, 2.22.1 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Advisory](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/security/advisories/GHSA-5jmj-h7xm-6q6v)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/commit/0e1b0b211f7a53baa62ba2f4c9bd006c7bf4d5fa)\n- [GitHub Issue](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/issues/5962)\n- [GitHub Issue](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/issues/5964)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-915",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.9,
                "security-severity": "6.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-COMFASTERXMLJACKSONCORE-17972437",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Improperly Controlled Modification of Dynamically-Determined Object Attributes vulnerability in com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-59888) com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind@2.15.4"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind) is a library which contains the general-purpose data-binding functionality and tree-model for Jackson Data Processor.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improperly Controlled Modification of Dynamically-Determined Object Attributes in the `POJOPropertiesCollector._removeUnwantedIgnorals` process. An attacker can access or modify properties that were intended to be ignored by supplying JSON input with keys matching the renamed property names, thereby bypassing intended access restrictions.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind` to version 2.18.8, 2.21.4 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Advisory](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/security/advisories/GHSA-3pjw-73gf-8qr5)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/commit/baa2cdf5ca2b2717fbb88d91955d69d8651df3e4)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/commit/c7c678360624da5bc7eed2152789fa522880db9d)\n- [GitHub PR](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/pull/5974)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-915",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.9,
                "security-severity": "6.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-COMFASTERXMLJACKSONCORE-19256875",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Server-side Request Forgery (SSRF) vulnerability in com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-77310) com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind@2.15.4"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind) is a library which contains the general-purpose data-binding functionality and tree-model for Jackson Data Processor.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Server-side Request Forgery (SSRF) through the `STD_INET_ADDRESS` branch in `FromStringDeserializer` in `src/main/java/com/fasterxml/jackson/databind/deser/std/FromStringDeserializer.java`. An attacker can trigger outbound DNS lookups and blind SSRF behavior by supplying a hostname string in JSON that is deserialized into `java.net.InetAddress`. When application code binds untrusted input into an `InetAddress` field or type, the deserializer calls `InetAddress.getByName(value)` on the attacker-controlled string and resolves it before any application validation runs. This lets an attacker force DNS-based callbacks or probe internal hostnames, causing unwanted network egress and leaking resolver-visible information.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind` to version 2.18.9, 2.21.5, 2.22.1 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit jackson-databind-2.21.1](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/commit/331c4a8ef8616a9f2581dd990bd6b9e9d8bca68b)\n- [GitHub Commit jackson-databind-3.2.1](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/commit/2fc7bd9057dd051d7dea0e5fcad89822d0fa5ebd)\n- [Maintainer's Advisory](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/security/advisories/GHSA-vvgp-rfg2-7rr6)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-918",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.9,
                "security-severity": "6.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-IOMICROMETER-17260885",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling vulnerability in io.micrometer:micrometer-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-40984) io.micrometer:micrometer-core@1.12.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling via HTTP server metrics instrumentation in Micrometer. An attacker can cause denial of service by sending specially crafted HTTP requests that trigger excessive resource consumption during metrics collection and processing. Repeated requests can degrade application performance and potentially render the service unavailable.\r\n\r\n**Note:** This is only exploitable if the application has one or more HTTP server instrumentations enabled with metrics collection configured.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `io.micrometer:micrometer-core` to version 1.15.12, 1.16.6 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/micrometer-metrics/micrometer/commit/36da131525228188a36779a28471a76c79213dd4)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-40984)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-770",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.2,
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-IOMICROMETER-19233327",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - CRLF Injection vulnerability in io.micrometer:micrometer-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-59296) io.micrometer:micrometer-core@1.12.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to CRLF Injection through `DatadogStatsdLineBuilder`, `EtsyStatsdLineBuilder`, and the `Printer` in `LoggingMeterRegistry`. An attacker can spoof metrics or log entries by supplying meter names, tag keys, or tag values containing `\\n` or `\\r`, causing the generated StatsD or log output to break into additional lines.\r\n\r\n**Notes**\r\n\r\n- Additional fixes are available for earlier versions under Enterprise Support (see the Spring Security Advisory for additional details)\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `io.micrometer:micrometer-core` to version 1.16.7, 1.17.1 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/micrometer-metrics/micrometer/commit/21095149cbb82b914bd9c0688a1622a4a3220f85)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-59296)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-93",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.2,
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-IOMICROMETER-19256585",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Missing Release of Memory after Effective Lifetime vulnerability in io.micrometer:micrometer-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-59295) io.micrometer:micrometer-core@1.12.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Missing Release of Memory after Effective Lifetime via the `MicrometerHttpClientInterceptor`. An attacker can cause unbounded memory consumption by repeatedly triggering asynchronous request failures before receiving a response, such as through connection resets or timeouts. This can ultimately lead to heap exhaustion and application crashes.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `io.micrometer:micrometer-core` to version 1.16.7, 1.17.1 or higher.\n## References\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-59295)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-401",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.2,
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHELOGGINGLOG4J-17954276",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Improper Encoding or Escaping of Output vulnerability in org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-api"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-49844) org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-api@2.21.1"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Encoding or Escaping of Output in the `MapMessage.asJson()` method, which emits the bare `NaN`, `Infinity`, or `-Infinity` tokens instead of an RFC 8259-compliant representation. An attacker can emit malformed JSON that corrupts the enclosing log record or disrupts downstream log ingestion and parsing by supplying non-finite floating-point values that the application records in a logged `MapMessage`. Exploitation requires the application to use the `message` resolver of `JsonTemplateLayout`, or another layout relying on `MapMessage.asJson()`, and to log a `MapMessage` holding attacker-controlled floating-point values.\n\n**Note:** This is a bypass of the fix for the vulnerability described in [CVE-2026-34481](https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHELOGGINGLOG4J-15967756).\n## Remediation\nA fix was pushed into the `master` branch but not yet published.\n## References\n- [event-template-resolver-message Documentation](https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/manual/json-template-layout.html#event-template-resolver-message)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/logging-log4j2/commit/19edb23e162d6c728a8c2221a240037d389ed300)\n- [GitHub PR](https://github.com/apache/logging-log4j2/pull/4163)\n- [Vulnerability Advisory](https://logging.apache.org/security.html#CVE-2026-49844)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-116",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.3,
                "security-severity": "6.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-10264469",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Improper Handling of Case Sensitivity vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-46701) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Handling of Case Sensitivity in the `pathInfo` component of a URI mapped to the CGI servlet. An attacker can bypass security constraints that apply to the `pathInfo` component by exploiting this vulnerability on a case insensitive file system.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.105, 10.1.41, 11.0.7 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Advisory](https://lists.apache.org/thread/xhqqk9w5q45srcdqhogdk04lhdscv30j)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_10.1.41)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_11.0.7)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-9.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_9.0.105)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/0f01966eb60015d975525019e12a087f05ebf01a)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/238d2aa54b99f91d1111467e2237d2244c64e558)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/2c6800111e7d8d8d5403c07978ea9bff3db5a5a5)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/8cb95ff03221067c511b3fa66d4f745bc4b0a605)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/8df00018a252baa9497615d6420fb6c10466fa74)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/fab7247d2f0e3a29d5daef565f829f383e10e5e2)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-178",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.3,
                "security-severity": "6.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-10365122",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-48988) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling due to the uniform handling of request parameters and parts in multipart requests. An attacker can craft a malicious request with a large number of parts, which can lead to a Denial of Service.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.106, 10.1.42, 11.0.8 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-9.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Thread](https://lists.apache.org/thread/nzkqsok8t42qofgqfmck536mtyzygp18)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/2b0ab14fb55d4edc896e5f1817f2ab76f714ae5e)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/cdde8e655bc1c5c60a07efd216251d77c52fd7f6)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/ee8042ffce4cb9324dfd79efda5984f37bbb6910)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-770",
