            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-8073090",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2024-38286) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling via the `unwrap()` function in `SecureNio2Channel` class, during a TLS handshake. Under certain configurations using TLS 1.3, an attacker can trigger an `OutOfMemoryError`.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.90, 10.1.25, 11.0.0-M21 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Tomcat 10 Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_10.1.25)\n- [Apache Tomcat 11 Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_11.0.0-M21)\n- [Apache Tomcat 9 Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-9.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_9.0.90)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/3197862639732e16ec1164557bcd289ebc116c93)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/3344c17cef094da4bb616f4186ed32039627b543)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/76c5cce6f0bcef14b0c21c38910371ca7d322d13)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-770",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.7,
                "security-severity": "8.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-8383920",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Uncaught Exception vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2024-52316) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Uncaught Exception due to the custom Jakarta Authentication `ServerAuthContext` component which may throw an exception during the authentication process without setting an HTTP status to indicate failure. An attacker can gain unauthorized access by exploiting this unchecked error condition.\r\n\r\n**Note:**\r\n\r\nThis is only exploitable if Tomcat is configured to use a custom Jakarta Authentication\r\n`ServerAuthContext` component that behaves in this way. According to the maintainers, no such cases are known.\n## PoC\n```python\r\nimport requests\r\n\r\n# Target server configuration\r\nTARGET_URL = \"http://example.com/login\"  # Replace with your target's authentication URL\r\nTEST_HEADERS = {\r\n    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\r\n}\r\nTEST_PAYLOAD = {\r\n    \"username\": \"test_user\",  # Sample username\r\n    \"password\": \"invalid_password\"  # Invalid password for testing\r\n}\r\n\r\ndef check_cve_2024_52316(target_url):\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    Test for CVE-2024-52316 vulnerability by sending crafted authentication requests.\r\n\r\n    Args:\r\n        target_url (str): The URL of the authentication endpoint to test.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    try:\r\n        print(f\"[*] Sending test request to {target_url}\")\r\n        # Send a POST request with the test payload\r\n        response = requests.post(target_url, json=TEST_PAYLOAD, headers=TEST_HEADERS, timeout=5)\r\n        \r\n        # Analyze the server's response\r\n        if response.status_code in [401, 403]:\r\n            print(f\"[SAFE] The server returned an expected HTTP status code: {response.status_code}\")\r\n        elif response.status_code == 200:\r\n            print(f\"[VULNERABLE] Potential CVE-2024-52316 detected! Server returned status code: {response.status_code}\")\r\n        else:\r\n            print(f\"[INFO] Unexpected HTTP status code: {response.status_code}\")\r\n            print(\"Response content:\", response.text)\r\n    except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\r\n        print(f\"[ERROR] Failed to connect to the target: {e}\")\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    print(\"[START] CVE-2024-52316 Detection Script\")\r\n    check_cve_2024_52316(TARGET_URL)\r\n```\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.96, 10.1.31, 11.0.0 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Advisory](https://lists.apache.org/thread/lopzlqh91jj9n334g02om08sbysdb928)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/6d097a66746635df6880fe7662a792156b0eca14)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/7532f9dc4a8c37ec958f79dc82c4924a6c539223)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/acc2f01395f895980f5d8a64573fcc1bade13369)\n- [PoC](http://github.com/TAM-K592/CVE-2024-52316)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-248",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.2,
                "security-severity": "9.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-8523186",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2024-50379) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition. On case insensitive file systems, when the default servlet is write-enabled, an attacker can upload a malicious file containing executable code and bypass case sensitivity checks, causing it to be treated as a JSP and executed.\r\n\r\nThis vector has been observed when the application is under load and read and upload operations are performed on the same file simultaneously.\r\n\r\n**Note:**\r\n\r\nThe default `readonly` initialization parameter value of `true` is not vulnerable.\r\n\r\nThis is related to [CVE-2024-56337](https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCAT-8547998) where additional configurations are defined to fully mitigate this issue as upgrading to the fixed version doesn't fully mitigate this vulnerability;\r\n\r\nIn addition to upgrading to the fixed version, users are advised to apply the following mitigations, depending on which version of Java they are using with Tomcat :\r\n\r\n1) running on Java 8 or Java 11: the system property `sun.io.useCanonCaches` must be explicitly set to false (it defaults\r\nto true)\r\n\r\n2) running on Java 17: the system property `sun.io.useCanonCaches`, if set, must be set to false (it defaults to false)\r\n\r\n3) running on Java 21 onwards: no further configuration is required (the system property and the problematic cache have been removed)\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.98, 10.1.34, 11.0.2 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Advisory](https://lists.apache.org/thread/y6lj6q1xnp822g6ro70tn19sgtjmr80r)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_10.1.34)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_11.0.2)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-9.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_9.0.98)\n- [Blog Post](https://medium.com/@patelvidhi4288/deep-dive-poc-of-cve-2024-50379-exploit-tomcat-vulnerability-9-8-severity-776cfcfcf3ed)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/05ddeeaa54df1e2dc427d0164bedd6b79f78d81f)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/43b507ebac9d268b1ea3d908e296cc6e46795c00)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/631500b0c9b2a2a2abb707e3de2e10a5936e5d41)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/684247ae85fa633b9197b32391de59fc54703842)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/8554f6b1722b33a2ce8b0a3fad37825f3a75f2d2)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/cc7a98b57c6dc1df21979fcff94a36e068f4456c)\n- [PoC in GitHub](https://github.com/iSee857/CVE-2024-50379-PoC)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-367",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.2,
                "security-severity": "9.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-8547999",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2024-56337) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition due to imcomplete mitigation advice associated with [CVE-2024-50379](https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCAT-8523184) in the file-handling process with servlet write enabled.\r\n\r\nIn addition to upgrading to the fixed version, users are advised to apply the following mitigations, depending on which version of Java they are using with Tomcat :\r\n\r\n1) running on Java 8 or Java 11: the system property `sun.io.useCanonCaches` must be explicitly set to false (it defaults to true)\r\n\r\n2) running on Java 17: the system property `sun.io.useCanonCaches`, if set, must be set to false (it defaults to false)\r\n\r\n3) running on Java 21 onwards: no further configuration is required (the system property and the problematic cache have been removed)\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.98, 10.1.34, 11.0.2 or higher.\n## References\n- [Additional Protection](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/0c75cd1e3ac85944fb8ecbcf88cc38e9fa1fe4d5)\n- [Apache Thread](https://lists.apache.org/thread/b2b9qrgjrz1kvo4ym8y2wkfdvwoq6qbp)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_10.1.34)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_11.0.2)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-9.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_9.0.98)\n- [Follow-up PR](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/pull/858)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/43b507ebac9d268b1ea3d908e296cc6e46795c00)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/631500b0c9b2a2a2abb707e3de2e10a5936e5d41)\n- [PoC](https://github.com/SleepingBag945/CVE-2024-50379)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-367",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.2,
                "security-severity": "9.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-9396739",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Path Equivalence vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-24813) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Path Equivalence in the `doPut()` function in `DefaultServlet.java`, which insecurely replaces path separators with `.`s. \r\n\r\nIf the Default Servlet is configured with writes enabled - which it is not by default - a user can exploit Tomcat's partial `PUT` functionality to achieve code execution via deserialization. The target URL containing sensitive uploaded files must be a sub-directory of a target URL for public uploads, and the malicious user must know the names of the target sensitive files, which are also uploaded using a partial `PUT`. If both attacker and target application are using the default storage location and it contains a library that deserializes untrusted code, the attacker can trigger the execution of malicious code.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.99, 10.1.35, 11.0.3 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/0a668e0c27f2b7ca0cc7c6eea32253b9b5ecb29c)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/eb61aade8f8daccaecabf07d428b877975622f72)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/f6c01d6577cf9a1e06792be47e623d36acc3b5dc)\n- [OSS Security Advisory](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/03/10/5)\n- [PoC](https://github.com/iSee857/CVE-2025-24813-PoC/blob/main/Tomcat_CVE-2025-24813_RCE.py)\n- [Nuclei Templates](https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/cves/2025/CVE-2025-24813.yaml)\n- [CISA - Known Exploited Vulnerabilities](https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog)\n- [Exploit DB](https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/52134)\n- [PoC in GitHub](https://github.com/qzy0x/cve-2025-24813_poc)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-44",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.7,
                "security-severity": "7.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-9905132",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Improper Cleanup on Thrown Exception vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-31650) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Cleanup on Thrown Exception when handling failed HTTP/2 requests with certain invalid HTTP priority headers. An attacker can trigger an `OutOfMemoryException` by sending a large number of malicious requests.\r\n\r\n**Note:** The project maintainers note that version 9.0.103 also fixes the vulnerability but was never officially released.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.104, 10.1.40, 11.0.6 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/j6zzk0y3yym9pzfzkq5vcyxzz0yzh826)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-9.html)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/1eef1dc459c45f1e421d8bd25ef340fc1cc34edc)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/40ae788c2e64d018b4e58cd4210bb96434d0100d)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/75554da2fc5574862510ae6f0d7b3d78937f1d40)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/8cc3b8fb3f2d8d4d6a757e014f19d1fafa948a60)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/b7674782679e1514a0d154166b1d04d38aaac4a9)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/b98e74f517b36929f4208506e5adad22cb767baa)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/cba1a0fe1289ee7f5dd46c61c38d1e1ac5437bff)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/ded0285b96b4d3f5560dfc8856ad5ec4a9b50ba9)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/f619e6a05029538886d5a9d987925d573b5bb8c2)\n- [OSS Security Advisory](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/04/28/2)\n- [PoC](https://github.com/nomi-sec/PoC-in-GitHub/tree/master/2025/CVE-2025-31650.json)\n- [Exploit DB](https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/52318)\n- [PoC in GitHub](https://github.com/absholi7ly/TomcatKiller-CVE-2025-31650)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-460",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.7,
                "security-severity": "8.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-9905136",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Improper Neutralization vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-31651) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization in the `RewriteValve` class, which handles rewrite rules. If rewrite rules are configured to enforce security constraints, those security constraints can be bypassed in some cases by sending a malicious request involving `;` or `?` characters.\r\n\r\n**Note:** The project maintainers note that version 9.0.103 also fixes the vulnerability but was never officially released.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.104, 10.1.40, 11.0.6 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/cpklvqwvdrp4k9hmd2l3q33j0gzy4fox)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-9.html)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/066bf6b6a15a4e7e0941d4acf096841165b97098)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/175dc75fc428930034a6c93fb52f830d955d8e64)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/ee3ab548e92345eca0cbd1f01649eb36c6f29454)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/fbecc915a10c5a3d634c5e2c6ced4ff479ce9953)\n- [OSS Security Advisory](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/04/28/3)\n- [PoC](https://github.com/nomi-sec/PoC-in-GitHub/tree/master/2025/CVE-2025-31651.json)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-150",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.3,
                "security-severity": "6.3"
              }
