            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-8230373",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Path Traversal vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-webmvc"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2024-38819) org.springframework:spring-webmvc@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.springframework:spring-webmvc](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.springframework/spring-webmvc) is a package that provides Model-View-Controller (MVC) architecture and ready components that can be used to develop flexible and loosely coupled web applications.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Path Traversal through the functional web frameworks `WebMvc.fn` or `WebFlux.fn`. An attacker can craft malicious HTTP requests and obtain any file on the file system that is also accessible.\r\n\r\n**Note:**\r\nThis is similar to [CVE-2024-38816](https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-7945490), but with different input.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-webmvc` to version 6.1.14 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/fb7890d73975a3d9e0763e0926df2bd0a608e87e)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2024-38819)\n- [PoC in GitHub](https://github.com/masa42/CVE-2024-38819-POC)\n- [Nuclei Templates](https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/cves/2024/CVE-2024-38819.yaml)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-23",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.7,
                "security-severity": "8.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-17253311",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Inefficient Algorithmic Complexity vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-expression"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-41850) org.springframework:spring-expression@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Inefficient Algorithmic Complexity via evaluation of user-controlled Spring Expression Language (SpEL) expressions. An attacker can cause denial of service by supplying specially crafted SpEL expressions that trigger excessive CPU or memory consumption during expression evaluation, leading to application degradation or unavailability.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-expression` to version 6.0.0, 6.2.19, 7.0.8 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/2c18c33ce0f89bf718c184190cfb7ed49b4276fb)\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v6.2.19)\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v7.0.8)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-41850)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-407",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.7,
                "security-severity": "8.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-17253570",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Exposed Dangerous Method or Function vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-expression"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-41852) org.springframework:spring-expression@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Exposed Dangerous Method or Function via Spring Expression Language (SpEL) method invocation handling. An attacker can invoke arbitrary zero-argument methods by supplying crafted SpEL expressions, even in contexts intended to restrict method execution or provide read-only access. This may allow execution of unintended application logic and access to functionality that should not be exposed through expression evaluation.\r\n\r\n**Note:** This is only exploitable if the application accepts and evaluates untrusted or user-controlled SpEL expressions.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-expression` to version 6.0.0, 6.2.19, 7.0.8 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/3d47da9746d54775a282717b539924f9e6e39096)\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v6.2.19)\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v7.0.8)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-41852)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-749",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.9,
                "security-severity": "6.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-18326606",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-expression"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-41851) org.springframework:spring-expression@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\n[org.springframework:spring-expression](https://search.maven.org/artifact/org.springframework/spring-expression/5.3.2/jar) is a \n\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling.\nvia caching of parsed Spring Expression Language (SpEL) expressions. An attacker can cause denial of service by supplying crafted user-controlled SpEL expressions that trigger unbounded growth of the expression cache. Over time, repeated evaluations can consume excessive memory, eventually leading to memory exhaustion and application unavailability.\r\n\r\n**Note:** Exploitation typically requires a large number of expression evaluations, potentially millions of requests, even when reusing a single expression with dynamic inputs.\n\n## Remediation\n\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-expression` to version 6.0.0, 6.2.19, 7.0.8 or higher.\n\n\n## References\n\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/85c578b929dc39c78026ba709c516e17268e6db0)\n\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v6.2.19)\n\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v7.0.8)\n\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-41851/)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-770",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.2,
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-19267073",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-expression"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-47886) org.springframework:spring-expression@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling in the evaluation of user-supplied SpEL expressions containing the power operator `(^)` with a `BigDecimal` or `BigInteger` operand and a large exponent value. An attacker can cause excessive CPU and memory consumption by submitting specially crafted expressions.\n\n**Note:** This is only exploitable if the application accepts and evaluates untrusted SpEL expressions and a `BigDecimal` or `BigInteger` value is accessible within the evaluation context.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-expression` to version 7.0.9 or higher.\n## References\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-47886)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-770",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.2,
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-19267075",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-expression"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-59283) org.springframework:spring-expression@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling in the `SimpleEvaluationContext` file when the SpEL expression compiler is enabled through specific configuration settings. An attacker can cause unbounded class-loading growth and bypass enforced safety checks by submitting specially crafted expressions for evaluation.\n\n**Note:** This is only exploitable if the application evaluates SpEL expressions using `SimpleEvaluationContext` and the SpEL expression compiler is active via the `spring.expression.compiler.mode` property or a `SpelParserConfiguration` set to `IMMEDIATE` or `MIXED`.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-expression` to version 7.0.9 or higher.\n## References\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-59283)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-770",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.3,
                "security-severity": "8.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORKBOOT-15701835",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Authentication Bypass Using an Alternate Path or Channel vulnerability in org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator-autoconfigure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-22733) org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator-autoconfigure@3.2.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Authentication Bypass Using an Alternate Path or Channel via the Actuator CloudFoundry endpoints. An attacker can gain unauthorized access to protected endpoints by sending requests to application endpoints declared under the CloudFoundry Actuator path.\r\n\r\n**Note:**\r\n\r\nThis is only exploitable if all of the following conditions are met:\r\n\r\n- the application is a web application\r\n\r\n- the application contributes an application endpoint that requires authentication under a subpath, like `\"/cloudfoundryapplication/admin\"`\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator-autoconfigure` to version 3.5.12, 4.0.4 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/commit/01fbede2b27237616e215fe0df7c294ae47bdd73)\n- [Spring Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-22733)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-288",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.2,
                "security-severity": "9.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORKBOOT-9804539",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Improper Input Validation vulnerability in org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator-autoconfigure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-22235) org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator-autoconfigure@3.2.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Input Validation via the `EndpointRequest.to()` function that creates a matcher for `null/**` if the actuator endpoint, for which the `EndpointRequest` has been created, is disabled or not exposed.\r\n\r\n**Note:**\r\n\r\nThis is only exploitable if all of the following conditions are met:\r\n\r\n1) `EndpointRequest.to()` has been used in a Spring Security chain configuration;\r\n\r\n2) The endpoint which `EndpointRequest` references is disabled or not exposed via web;\r\n\r\n3) Your application handles requests to `/null` and this path needs protection.\r\n\r\n## Workaround\r\n\r\nThis can be mitigated by either:\r\n\r\n1) Making sure that the endpoint to which `EndpointRequest.to()` is referring to is enabled and exposed via web;\r\n\r\n2) Make sure that you don't handle requests to `/null`.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator-autoconfigure` to version 3.3.11, 3.4.5 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/commit/55f67c9a522647039fd3294dee5cb83f4888160a)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2025-22235)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-20",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.9,
                "security-severity": "6.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORKBOOT-15701836",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Authentication Bypass Using an Alternate Path or Channel vulnerability in org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-22733) org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator@3.2.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Authentication Bypass Using an Alternate Path or Channel via the Actuator CloudFoundry endpoints. An attacker can gain unauthorized access to protected endpoints by sending requests to application endpoints declared under the CloudFoundry Actuator path.\r\n\r\n**Note:**\r\n\r\nThis is only exploitable if all of the following conditions are met:\r\n\r\n- the application is a web application\r\n\r\n- the application contributes an application endpoint that requires authentication under a subpath, like `\"/cloudfoundryapplication/admin\"`\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator` to version 3.5.12, 4.0.4 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/commit/01fbede2b27237616e215fe0df7c294ae47bdd73)\n- [Spring Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-22733)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
