            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORKBOOT-16191022",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Improper Validation of Certificate with Host Mismatch vulnerability in org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-40974) org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure@3.2.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Validation of Certificate with Host Mismatch due to establishing SSL connections to Cassandra without verifying that the hostname in the server's SSL certificate actually matched the hostname of the server being connected to. While the application might have verified that the certificate was signed by a trusted Certificate Authority (CA), failing to verify the hostname means an attacker could present any valid certificate (even one meant for a different domain) to successfully intercept the connection, leaving the application vulnerable to Man-in-the-Middle (MitM) attacks.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure` to version 3.5.14, 4.0.6 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/commit/e22083a5684c3c65bcf2a9a90adcdecee6e85d50)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-40974)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-297",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.3,
                "security-severity": "9.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORKBOOT-16200231",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Improper Validation of Certificate with Host Mismatch vulnerability in org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-40971) org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure@3.2.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Validation of Certificate with Host Mismatch when using an SSL bundle. This effectively weakens TLS by allowing connections without verifying the server identity (classic MITM risk).\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure` to version 3.5.14, 4.0.6 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/commit/e4febe2015d340ea9135437ee0659ea0f2260c31)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-40971)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
